 be true in the case of low acceleration efficiency, in which only left-hand modes are excited). In addition to the waves that can resonate with protons, the right-hand branch also has modes that grow for $kr_{L,0} \geq 1$ , as discussed above. For the set of parameters used in Fig. 9, the maximum growth occurs for $k_{*}r_{L,0} \sim 10^{4}$ . One can also notice how the real part of the frequency of the fast growing modes is very small: these modes are basically almost purely growing. ![](images/7f04dbd5468184a549a1b58e69b391958867049e7e32744e7949206b0c969782.jpg)  
